<surname>Christensen</surname><given-names>FM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pharmaceuticals in the environment &#x02013; a human risk?</article-title><source>Regul Toxicol Pharmacol</source><year>1998</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>212</fpage><lpage>221</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10049792</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/rtph.1998.1253</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Woodward</surname><given-names>KN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Veterinary Pharmacovigilance. Part 3. Adverse effects of veterinary medicinal products in animals and on the environment</article-title><source>J Vet Pharmacol Therap</source><year>2005</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>171</fpage><lpage>184</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15842306</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1365-2885.2005.00647.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boxall</surname><given-names>ABA</given-names></name><name><surname>Kolpin</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>Halling-Sorensen</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Tolls</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Are veterinary medicines causing environmental risk?</article-title><source>Environ Sci Techno</source><year>2003</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>286</fpage><lpage>294A</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Richard</surname><given-names>WilliamsT</given-names></name><name><surname>Cook</surname><given-names>JonC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Exposure to Pharmaceuticals Present in the Environment</article-title><source>Drug Information Journal</source><year>2007</year><volume>41</volume><fpage>133</fpage><lpage>141</lpage></citati